<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kassel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kassel is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulda">Fulda</a> river. It was the residence of the landgraves of Hesse and from 1567 the capital of Hesse-Kassel, later the Electorate of Hesse, and from 1807 to 1813 the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brothers-grimm">Brothers Grimm</a> worked there, and the city is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergpark-wilhelmshohe">Bergpark Wilhelmshöhe</a> and the documenta exhibitions of contemporary art.</p></div>
